<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22389v1/ipr_1.5_split_top1_lm.svg" id="A6.F29.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:224/84;" width="224" height="84"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22389v1/ipr_1.5_top2_split_lm.svg" id="A6.F29.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:224/84;" width="224" height="84"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 29: </span>Effective top-<math id="A6.F29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> for DNA-n models (language), as a function of number of forward pass steps <math id="A6.F29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. The trend is very different from the vision models we have shown earlier. <span id="A6.F29.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left</span>: top-1 DNA-n model. <span id="A6.F29.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right</span>: top-2 DNA-n model.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
